----------------------------------------------------------------------
Modifications in Fathom relative to upstream x64dbg
----------------------------------------------------------------------
- TraceExport            : export execution traces to JSON / CSV.
- pybridge               : drive the debugger from Python (plugin + client).
- headless templates     : ready-to-use scripts for headless.exe.
- ExtraCmds plugin       : .init / .save / scylla_hide.* convenience commands,
                           a minidump viewer, and the HvKdFusion commands; plus a
                           dockable "HvKdFusion" GUI tab.
- HvKdFusion             : Hyper-V kernel debugging and memory forensics
                           (hvkd*, and "wineye", a native WinDbg-style passive
                           memory REPL with MCP / DAP / gdbserver modes).
- emulator               : the emu.* commands of ExtraCmds and emulator/: code of
                           the debuggee run from a minidump in dumpulator
                           (vendored and modified, see emulator/README.md), with
                           emulated traces in x64dbg's trace format.
- Triton plugin          : the sym.* / taint.* commands (triton/): symbolic
                           execution and taint analysis with Triton (vendored
                           unmodified in triton/third_party/Triton) on the
                           debuggee or on a recorded trace, solved with Z3;
                           vm.* (the method of VMHunt, reimplemented).
- Decompiler plugin      : the decompile command (decompiler/): Ghidra's
                           decompiler (vendored in decompiler/third_party/ghidra,
                           one change: see FATHOM.md there) on the debuggee.
- analysis tools         : novmp (NoVmp + VTIL, novmp/, changed for today's
                           VTIL and ported to x86: see
                           novmp/third_party/FATHOM.md), angr.* and miasm.*
                           (analysis/, miasm vendored unmodified), remill.lift
                           (remill/, remill vendored, changed for Windows: see
                           remill/third_party/FATHOM.md), revng.decompile
                           (revng/: rev.ng vendored and ported to Windows, see
                           revng/third_party/FATHOM.md; rev.ng's fork of QEMU
                           changed: revng/patches/qemu.patch), binja and the
                           Binary Ninja plugin (binja/).
- plugin installer       : ScyllaHide / xAnalyzer / PE-sieve / OllyDumpEx, with
                           SHA-256 verification.
- build / release fixes  : minidump viewer CMAKE_SYSTEM_VERSION, unity build.
- branding               : launcher renamed to Fathom.exe with its own icon, the
                           main-window title and the version resource set to
                           "Fathom". The engine executables and DLLs keep their
                           x64dbg names (x64dbg.exe/x32dbg.exe, x64dbg.dll,
                           x64gui.dll, x64bridge.dll) because the plugin SDK and
                           all plugins depend on those names.

